---
const items = [
  {
    title: 'yassergandhi.dev',
    copy: 'SaaS and software flows where missing guidance becomes operating cost.',
    href: '/',
  },
  {
    title: 'huhuGERMAN',
    copy: 'Language, behavior, and scaffolded practice under real-world pressure.',
    href: 'https://huhugerman.com',
  },
  {
    title: 'Fernweh Together',
    copy: 'Forthcoming: shared experience design where the platform must guide the moment.',
    href: '',
  },
];
---
<section id="ecosystem">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Ecosystem</div>
    <h2>One authorial signature, three contexts where guidance disappears.</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">The proof is the same reading discipline applied across product systems, language systems, and shared experience systems.</p>
    <div class="ecosystem-grid">
      {items.map((item) => item.href ? (
        <a class="ecosystem-link" href={item.href} target={item.href.startsWith('http') ? '_blank' : undefined} rel={item.href.startsWith('http') ? 'noopener' : undefined}>
          <strong>{item.title}</strong>
          <span>{item.copy}</span>
        </a>
      ) : (
        <div class="ecosystem-link is-static">
          <span class="badge">forthcoming</span>
          <strong>{item.title}</strong>
          <span>{item.copy}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="section-copy ecosystem-line">When the system stops guiding, the real design begins.</p>
  </div>
</section>
